This is a "YANI", rgrn shorthad for, "I sure hope
someone else volunteers to do all the work", that
said "someone", or perhaps a "team of someones",
collects all the (usable / worthwhile / publicly
praised) rgrn rationalizations over time for how
weird stuff in NetHack "really, really" makes sense
if you just look at it from the appropriately
severely warped perspective, and turns that
collection into some conveniently accessible "stuff"
with the status and accessibility of the spoilers
files or the FAQ.

There have been lots and lots of such sub-threads
over time in rgrn, winkling them all out would be a
definite job of work.

Correlated with this should be a list of "to be
rationalized" glaringly counterintuitive NetHack
features, a basis from which to prod future
contributions in this direction.

This could, I suspect, be a fun "for the community"
project for someone / some group.

